--TEST--
code that is not a test cannot call a `#[Test]`, a `#[Fixture]` or a class hook, because `nvs run` and `nvs build` compile none of them (`rule:testing/tests-never-reach-a-build`), and a type error inside a test is still reported
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Core\Test;
use Core\Test\Fixture;
use Core\Test\BeforeClass;

final class Cart {
    public function total(): int { return 0; }
}

final class CartTest {
    #[Fixture]
    public static function cart(): Cart { return new Cart(); }

    #[BeforeClass]
    public static function prepare(): void {}

    // A test may call a fixture, a hook and another test, and so may a
    // function written inside one.
    #[Test]
    public function anEmptyCartCostsNothing(Cart $cart): void {
        self::prepare();
        var $again = fn(): Cart => self::cart();
        Test::assertSame(0, $again()->total());
    }

    // A test is still type-checked.
    #[Test]
    public function aTotalIsAnInt(Cart $cart): void {
        string $total = $cart->total();
        Test::assertSame("0", $total);
    }

    // The class's other methods are not test code, so they cannot call it.
    public function helper(): Cart {
        return self::cart();
    }
}

// Neither can the program itself.
CartTest::prepare();
echo (new CartTest())->helper()->total();
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `int`
   --> case.nvs:29:25
%A
error[E0889]: `CartTest::cart` is test code, so only a test can call it
   --> case.nvs:35:16
%A
error[E0889]: `CartTest::prepare` is test code, so only a test can call it
   --> case.nvs:40:1
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
